      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author constructs reciprocal parallelisms on adapted frame bundles and identifies their differential Galois obstructions with those of the D-Lie algebra. Vanishing of the Galois Lie algebra is then converted into an algebraic covering on which the groupoid descends from a homogeneous-space action, retaining the rational-integrability theorem and its construction. This combines differential algebra, algebraic groupoids and descent beyond ordinary qualifying-exam applications.",
